WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.080
The SCP Foundation’s existence might be
a frightening thing to some, but if you ask

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.299
us, it’s comforting.

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:12.299
Of course, the existence of the Foundation
implies the existence of all the mind-meltingly

00:00:12.299 --> 00:00:17.700
terrifying entities they combat on a daily
basis, but doesn’t it put your mind at least

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.019
a little at ease to know somebody out there
knows what’s going on?

00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:26.430
After all, sometimes, knowledge is the only
light we have in the darkness.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:32.300
It’s humanity’s greatest strength, to
know things and to act accordingly.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:37.730
From knowledge, we can understand our enemies
and the threats they pose against us.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.020
From knowledge, we can build sturdier defences.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.980
From knowledge, we can develop the means to
finally, effectively strike back.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:51.820
And nobody among the ranks of humanity has
more knowledge than the SCP Foundation.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:56.370
So what happens when the knowledge of the
SCP Foundation fails us?

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:00.899
What happens when a concept eludes even them?

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:07.259
A concept like, say, SCP-2317, an old wooden
door that hides within a truly terrible secret

00:01:07.259 --> 00:01:13.050
- A secret known by many as the Devourer Of
Worlds, a beast every bit as powerful and

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.030
unpleasant as that name suggests.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:21.530
The SCP Foundation performs a complex set
of rituals every single day to keep him contained,

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:27.220
and if the top brass of the Foundation is
to be believed, then these rituals are effective.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:32.250
But I think we all know better than to believe
everything we’re told around here, don’t

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.250
we?

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:39.240
The truth is this: Beyond the wooden door
known as SCP-2317, there’s a hellish desert

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.300
world, underneath which the Devourer of Worlds
awaits.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.520
He is kept in place, bound by ancient chains
created by a race that has long since been

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.530
lost to the history books.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:53.969
And while the Foundation tells its underlings
that the rituals D-Class personnel perform

00:01:53.969 --> 00:02:00.640
here every day helps to keep these chains
in place, this is little more than a placebo.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.049
The rituals only exist to make the Foundation
feel like they’re doing something to bide

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:09.369
time, while they figure out an actual lasting
solution.

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:14.160
In reality, based on the Foundation’s current
knowledge, these chains could break any day

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.150
now - and sadly, there’s nothing they can
do about it.

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:24.410
This may seem like the worst possible truth
to learn, but we can think of one even worse

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.069
truth: That “any day now”...

00:02:27.069 --> 00:02:28.860
Is today.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:34.010
When the chain breaks, the ground begins to
rumble worldwide, like an earthquake so great

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.700
it might even split the planet in two.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:41.180
No conventional scientist anywhere in the
world has any idea what’s happening, but

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.430
the SCP Foundation does.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:48.620
For the first time in recorded history, the
entire O5 Council are quaking.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:54.250
It’s judgment day, and their every sin is
on an express trip back to get them.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:59.760
They put out a call to dispatch every single
Mobile Task Force, worldwide, to come to Site

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.030
19 and combat the new threat.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.170
But deep down, the council members silently
worried this would be about as effective as

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:10.739
the sham rituals they claimed every day would
protect them.

00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:13.700
Meanwhile, Site 19 exploded.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:18.709
Most of the Foundation personnel and anomalies
stationed there perished in an instance, as

00:03:18.709 --> 00:03:23.890
a giant clawed hand rose out of the ground,
grasping at the sunlight for the first time

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:27.069
in millions of years since imprisonment.

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:33.030
Its sheer size - hundreds of kilometers in
height - displaces and destroys the land around

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.210
it as it climbs free from the earth.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:40.680
The Devourer Of Worlds is a monster of such
magnitude that it dwarfs even the Foundation’s

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:46.760
mightiest weapons, but their Mobile Task Forces
fight valiantly - or perhaps, foolishly - nonetheless.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:52.780
The Foundation went in with its finest resources
and weaponry, from advanced cruise missiles

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:57.220
to classified laser projectile weapons that
conventional militaries wouldn’t be finding

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:58.830
for another century.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:03.360
And all of it amounted to about the strength
of getting a mid-rate birthday clown’s cheap

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.569
cream pie to the face.

00:04:05.569 --> 00:04:10.019
The thick, scaly hide of the beast somehow
rejected everything they threw at it.

00:04:10.019 --> 00:04:15.379
Jets were scrambled, flying around the Devourer’s
gargantuan head and peppering its great eye

00:04:15.379 --> 00:04:18.540
with bullets, followed by heat-guided rockets.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:19.540
Nothing.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:23.040
The monster simply swatted them out of the
air with its claws.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:28.370
Down below, ground forces mobilized en masse,
from tanks to turrets, unleashing all kinds

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:31.370
of hell onto the Devourer of Worlds from below.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.870
And still, what good did it do?

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:38.110
The monster simply kept walking, killing thousands
with every footfall.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:41.110
Its magnitude was simply unfathomable.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:46.590
Scranton Reality anchors were placed at its
feet, in hopes of creating some kind of trap,

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.240
but its ancient flesh defied their force.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:53.750
Every Mobile Task Force from Hammer Down to
Samsara did what they could, and what they

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:57.760
could do ultimately amounted to a fat lot
of nothing.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.360
The rampage of the Devourer was undeterred.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:06.380
Within an hour, he would reach a population
center, and then, true hell would be unleashed

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.460
upon the human race.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:13.770
But sometimes, the only thing that could destroy
something inhuman was something so much more

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:15.160
than human.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:20.970
Over in the low risk humanoid containment
center of Site 17, SCP-343, perhaps better

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:25.889
known as God, was watching all the horror
unfold in his mind’s eye.

00:05:25.889 --> 00:05:30.410
So the Devourer was finally free, and wreaking
havoc on the world that he’d put so much

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.210
effort into creating.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.880
No, no, that simply would not do.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:40.729
How could he let such a vulgar creature take
billions of years of beauty, love, kindness,

00:05:40.729 --> 00:05:45.220
happiness, and natural majesty, and turn it
all into ash and dust?

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.819
He would not stand for it.

00:05:47.819 --> 00:05:52.449
But God, while unimaginably powerful, is a
philosopher, not a warrior.

00:05:52.449 --> 00:05:57.660
It would be not only beneath his celestial
position, but dangerous for all life on Earth,

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:02.550
if he were to unleash the power required to
destroy the Devourer himself.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:07.410
The armies of God are the greatest in heaven
or earth, but he would need a champion to

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:08.479
lead them.

00:06:08.479 --> 00:06:13.930
And while the operatives of the SCP Foundation
fought and died bravely for the human race,

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:20.280
SCP-343 blipped out of Site 17, and reappeared
in the Middle East, where his champion would

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:24.080
be waiting, guarding the gate to paradise.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:28.039
SCP-001, in this case, known as The Gate Guardian.

00:06:28.039 --> 00:06:34.400
A huge, glowing humanoid with wings made of
fire, and a sword hotter than the sun, capable

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:37.330
of cleaving its enemies apart on the atomic
level.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:41.139
Typically, any being who traveled within a
kilometer of the Gate Guardian would receive

00:06:41.139 --> 00:06:46.780
this treatment - a strike so powerful that
in the aftermath, not even dust would remain.

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:52.169
But when SCP-343 appeared mere feet away from
the mighty Gate Guardian, the Guardian fell

00:06:52.169 --> 00:06:56.430
to one knee and bowed its glowing head in
holy reverence.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.610
“Master,” the Guardian said.

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:02.450
“You have returned to me, at long last.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:04.840
I will do thy bidding.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:06.760
What must be done?”

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.710
“Uriel,” God said, gravely.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:13.590
“An enemy is at the gates, one more powerful
than this world has ever known.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:16.750
Battle him, while I gather the armies.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.180
Do whatever it takes.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.360
He must be stopped.”

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:25.190
The Gate Guardian, Uriel, rose to his feet,
spreading his great wings of fire.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:31.670
“It shall be done, my Lord,” Uriel boomed,
and faster than any human being could possibly

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:37.170
perceive it, he had taken off into the sky,
leaving the gate behind him unguarded for

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:40.360
the first time in the memory of the human
race.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:41.639
God sighed.

00:07:41.639 --> 00:07:44.699
It was time to finally open it.

00:07:44.699 --> 00:07:49.380
Back with the Devourer, and the Mobile Task
Force army trying in vain to slow his advance.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:53.289
For the most part, the creature’s hide was
so thick, it was hard to even know if he noticed

00:07:53.289 --> 00:07:56.120
most of the puny humans firing on it.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:00.460
Some of the ones down below, driven half mad
with fear, rage, and the crushing weight of

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:05.539
futility, pulled out knives, swords, and bayonets
and ran at the creature’s feet, stabbing

00:08:05.539 --> 00:08:09.180
away even as their blades were blunted and
destroyed.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:13.819
Of course, the Devourer Of Worlds paid no
mind to them, it had something else in its

00:08:13.819 --> 00:08:18.210
sights: A human city, a mere handful of steps
away.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:24.360
Yes, yes, so teeming with life, such delicious
morsels.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:29.330
The Devourer would live up to his terrifying
namesake and feast on them all.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:33.810
Yes, yes, it would be... delicious.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:39.390
As he crushed further thousands of Mobile
Task Force soldiers below him just by walking,

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:41.209
he could hardly wait...

00:08:41.209 --> 00:08:44.140
Down below, things had never seemed so hopeless.

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:45.760
Was this how it ended?

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:51.170
One impotent last stand as a hungry monster
of inconceivable size bulldozed through life

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:55.640
and civilization and left nothing, nobody,
in its wake?

00:08:55.640 --> 00:09:00.601
Was this how the complicated but proud story
of the human race would come to an end, down

00:09:00.601 --> 00:09:03.350
here in the worthless, blood-soaked mud?

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:06.430
That’s when something changed.

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:11.519
The sky, once blotted out with the Devourer’s
shadow, was lit up by a brilliant, white light.

00:09:11.519 --> 00:09:17.920
A light so dazzling, so holy and pure, that
it gave even the Devourer pause.

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:21.800
The human beings down below wept with joy
and numinous awe.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:22.890
It was him.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:29.660
It was SCP-001, the Gate Guardian, spreading
his fiery wings and drawing his solar sword.

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:35.279
“My Master ordered me to destroy you,”
his deafening psychic voice boomed.

00:09:35.279 --> 00:09:38.980
“And thus, you shall be destroyed.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:42.070
Prepare to meet your maker.”

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:47.019
The Devourer immediately let out a world-shaking
roar, so powerful that many of the humans

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:51.589
down below felt their brains rattling and
their ears literally beginning to bleed.

00:09:51.589 --> 00:09:56.720
The beast reached for Uriel with its huge,
clawed hand, moving at impossible speeds for

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.529
a creature its size.

00:09:58.529 --> 00:10:00.300
Onlookers gasped in shock.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:06.050
Luckily, for as surprisingly fast as the Devourer
Of Worlds was, Uriel was faster.

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:10.120
Like the flash of an exploding lightbulb,
the Guardian darted out of the Devourer’s

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:14.970
palm and cleaved a glowing gash into the monster’s
wrist with his solar sword.

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:17.470
The creature growled, taken off guard.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:22.600
It was the first time in millions of years,
since it was attacked and bound by those impossible

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:26.370
celestial armies, that it had felt pain.

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:29.490
What was this mysterious warrior of fire?

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:33.420
All the Devourer knew was that if it wanted
to turn the planet earth into an all you can

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:38.779
eat buffet, it would need to do away with
this glowing nuisance first.

00:10:38.779 --> 00:10:40.040
“DIE!”

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:45.030
the psychic voice of the Gate Guardian commanded,
as it flew in for another strike, this time

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:49.360
cleaving into the beast’s torso and leaving
a long, glowing scar.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:51.070
But he didn’t stop there.

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:56.200
The Gate Guardian had changed posture from
a defensive, territorial stance to an all-out

00:10:56.200 --> 00:11:01.019
offensive warpath, as commanded by his all-powerful
master.

00:11:01.019 --> 00:11:06.490
Uriel was not arrogant, he could see that
the beast he was battling was undeniably formidable.

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:11.829
But he had slain formidable enemies before,
and he would do so again now.

00:11:11.829 --> 00:11:15.940
Taking advantage of the comparative slowness
and clunkiness of the Devourer - a natural

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:21.310
side effect of its truly immense size - Uriel
decided to stay mobile, flying around the

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:24.830
Devourer like an electron orbiting the nucleus
of an atom.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:29.760
At any moment that he, with his warrior’s
judgment, detected an opening, a weakness,

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:35.850
he flew in and struck with extreme fury, leaving
another glowing scar in the monster’s thick

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:39.510
scales that fizzled with the impossible heat
of his sword.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:44.170
Each time, the beast gave a grunt or a growl
in confused pain, as it desperately flailed

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:46.220
to try and grab the holy warrior.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:50.920
Meanwhile, the SCP Foundation had figured
out what was happening, and was reorienting

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:51.920
its focus.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:56.470
While the Gate Guardian fought against and
distracted the Devourer Of Worlds, all surviving

00:11:56.470 --> 00:12:01.200
Foundation personnel, under the instruction
of the O5 Council, converged on the nearest

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.030
city to the Devourer.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:07.340
They would evacuate as many as they could,
buying them more time to calculate some kind

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:12.399
of meaningful counteroffensive to this XK-Class
End of the World Scenario.

00:12:12.399 --> 00:12:17.471
If this really could be humanity’s last
stand, they would go out swinging, and leave

00:12:17.471 --> 00:12:19.510
their opponent with a black eye.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:24.470
While the evacuation efforts were underway,
Uriel continued his relentless assault against

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:28.790
the Devourer, carving scar after scar into
the monster’s body.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:33.279
He couldn’t tell if he was leaving much
lasting damage, but at the very least, he

00:12:33.279 --> 00:12:36.110
was getting the abomination’s attention.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:40.800
After striking its body countless times, though,
Uriel finally felt bold enough to go against

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:45.839
the creature’s obvious weak point: Its huge,
staring, cycloptic eye.

00:12:45.839 --> 00:12:49.830
Perhaps, with a decisive strike, he could
blind the beast.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:54.360
Faster than the speed of sound, Uriel orbited
the beast’s body, and reoriented himself

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:55.920
in front of its eye.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.920
He could feel the nanoseconds passing as he
charged, raising his sword.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.339
Now would be the time to end this.

00:13:02.339 --> 00:13:03.860
But wait... what’s that?

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:06.829
Why is the Devourer’s eye suddenly glowing
red?

00:13:06.829 --> 00:13:11.800
Before even Uriel had time to react, a tremendous
force of pure energy blasted forth from the

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:16.800
Devourer’s eye, bombarding the angelic soldier
and firing him straight into the ground below.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:21.360
He didn’t even know the monster possessed
such a power, and now, the force of it was

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.329
hammering him into the earth.

00:13:23.329 --> 00:13:28.040
The blast kept going for a few more seconds,
sapping Uriel’s strength and introducing

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:30.079
him to a long-forgotten pain.

00:13:30.079 --> 00:13:34.889
When the beam was done firing, Uriel felt
as though he could barely move.

00:13:34.889 --> 00:13:36.310
He was a sitting duck.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:41.449
That’s when the Devourer began marching
towards him, every step rattling the earth.

00:13:41.449 --> 00:13:44.360
Even as the threat loomed, Uriel couldn’t
move.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:45.930
Was this the end?

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:48.820
“Forgive me, Master,” Uriel said.

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:51.180
“I have failed you...”

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:56.420
Then, Uriel noticed something: Several projectiles
firing towards the Devourer’s head, seemingly

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.570
out of thin air.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:03.139
A volley of intercontinental ballistic missiles,
each equipped with a nuclear payload, exploded

00:14:03.139 --> 00:14:07.260
against the creature’s head, blasting it
with a shockwave that rattled the mighty creature

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:08.420
on its feet.

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:10.570
Had human beings made such weapons?

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:17.010
If they could still fight, even after all
this, Uriel thought, then I must fight too.

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:20.079
I must fight to my last breath!

00:14:20.079 --> 00:14:24.630
As the Devourer steadied itself, recovering
from the nuclear bombardment to the head,

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:29.899
Uriel rose with a terrifying warrior’s roar,
feeling his holy power return to him.

00:14:29.899 --> 00:14:35.500
His sword ignited and he charged forward,
faster than ever before, ready to strike clear

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.720
and true...

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:38.790
into the Devourer’s wretched heart.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:43.850
Before the beast could react, Uriel shoved
his sword into the center of its chest, causing

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:47.730
veins of agonizing flame to spread out over
its whole body.

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:51.890
At long last, he had well and truly harmed
the unharmable.

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:57.040
That knowledge sanctified him, even as the
Devourer Of Worlds grabbed Uriel in his fist,

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:01.610
and squeezed the life out of the warrior for
God for the last time.

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:04.910
Good, the Devourer thought, in its own way.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:07.480
I can finally carry on now.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:13.150
“You fought bravely, Uriel,” said a booming
voice from above the beast.

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:19.470
“Your sacrifice will not be in vain, that
much, I promise you.”

00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:25.260
Confused, the Devourer turned and looked skyward,
only to see a sight that struck pure and undiluted

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:30.220
awe into even him: It was God and his army.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:35.110
SCP-343 floated in the sky, lightning emanating
from his very being.

00:15:35.110 --> 00:15:39.290
Around him, glowing, angelic warriors, each
as large and as powerful as Uriel, and as

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:42.120
numerous as the stars in the sky above.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.750
God pointed at the Devourer.

